  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assisted Passage Travel and Related Services for Australian Government Funded Refugees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Organization for Migration (IOM) will continue to provide Assisted Passage (AP) services for sensitive cases in Thailand and the Cox&#x2019;s Bazar refugee camp in Bangladesh under its current agreement with the Department of Home Affairs (DHA). Due to ongoing civil unrest in Bangladesh, it is unlikely that Toll Group will be able to transition into the Cox&#x2019;s Bazar refugee camp soon. Consequently, DHA has requested IOM to continue providing AP services for three categories: Myanmar-sensitive and Rohingya cases in detention from Thailand, politically sensitive cases in Thailand, and the caseload from the Cox&#x2019;s Bazar refugee camp.This request exemplifies the critical role that IOM plays in managing and facilitating the movement of vulnerable populations, particularly during periods of political instability and civil unrest. The continuation of AP services by IOM will ensure that affected individuals receive the necessary support and assistance to safely relocate.</narrative>
  </description>
